From: wangra <wangra@google.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 20:20:22 -0400
Subject: D3D11: Backup texture storage contents on base level changes

Preserve subresource data when recreating texture storage on base level
change or release, preventing fast-path texture contents from being
dropped and avoiding uninitialized memory disclosure under robust
initialization.

Test:
    angle_end2end_tests --gtest_filter="SetBaseLevelPreservesFastPathSubImageData"
Bug: b/553117809, b/561613771
Change-Id: I4d688fa799e9ca48d1c4bd90216dd4b301726dc4
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/angle/angle/+/8377969
Commit-Queue: Ran Wang <wangra@google.com>
Reviewed-by: Shahbaz Youssefi <syoussefi@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Geoff Lang <geofflang@chromium.org>

Electron adaptation notes (42-x-y): TextureD3D::releaseTexStorage() on this
branch takes a single gl::TexLevelMask rather than a per-cube-face
gl::CubeFaceArray<gl::TexLevelMask>; the any-mask check and the per-image copy
test use that flat mask. Test-only hunks in TextureTest.cpp were dropped.

